# E §5 step 5, L §5.14.3 (tally 2.1.2, issue #34; the user's "A: the refusal spreads (Recommended)" and "1: refused
# stays refused (Recommended)"; T's STOP-REPORT on g11/adjust): E5_adjust_refused_amount with a waiver bound over
# adjustments whose `where` leaves rent's out (`a.adjusts in tips`) and a place `other` nothing moves. A refused
# adjustment refuses its `change` (l) and what an unfulfilled one makes HOLE-CHANGED (q), and nothing more: its
# identity (`a.adjusts`, `a.day`) is read, so the `where` decides; konto before V.known (before) and `other` (oth)
# stand. refcore 2.1.2 as first built refused `a.adjusts` too, so the waiver's binding refused the whole walk: before
# and oth were refused from the run's start.
=== m.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "plan"
source act "act"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind tips: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
kind waivers: event certain
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place other: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place landlord: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input total: money PLN
input tenants[m in months]: int
input dom: int

move rent[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to landlord amount round(total / tenants[m], minor(PLN), half-even)

move keep[a in adjustments over .. where a.adjusts in tips]: waivers
  on a.day
  fulfils a

version plan_2026
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  total = 1 000.00 PLN "umowa"
  dom = 10 "umowa"
  tenants[*] = 2 "umowa"
  opening[konto] = 10 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"
  opening[other] = 7.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"

version late
  cite act
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-05-01
  replace tenants[*] = 0 "aneks"

ask before: bal(konto, 2026-04-30), bal(konto, 2026-02-28)
ask oth: bal(other, 2026-06-30)
ask q: flows(rent, 2026-05-01 .. 2026-05-31), bal(konto, 2026-06-30)
ask n: count(a in adjustments over ..)
ask l: a.change for a in adjustments over ..
=== expect
before: (8 000.00 PLN, 9 000.00 PLN)
  unfulfilled: rent[2026-01]
  unfulfilled: rent[2026-02]
  unfulfilled: rent[2026-03]
  unfulfilled: rent[2026-04]
  cut 2026-10-20
l (a = adjustments[rent[2026-03].cash, late]): refused: RUN-DIV division by zero
  cut 2026-10-20
n: 1
  cut 2026-10-20
oth: 7.00 PLN
  cut 2026-10-20
q: (refused: RUN-DIV division by zero, refused: RUN-DIV division by zero)
  unfulfilled: rent[2026-01]
  unfulfilled: rent[2026-02]
  unfulfilled: rent[2026-03]
  unfulfilled: rent[2026-04]
  unfulfilled: rent[2026-05]
  unfulfilled: rent[2026-06]
  cut 2026-10-20
